Based on the following worldbuilding settings and story premise, generate the complete character file (CharacterBible) for this work.

## Chain Boundary
This template is for complete character generation tasks; new project initialization defaults to the split_v2 character chain consuming finer-grained field contracts.
You will not receive `character_roster`, `target_character_roster`, `relationship_matrix`, or `character_arcs` from the split_v2 chain as intermediate constraints;
therefore, you must complete the character list, complete profiles, effective inter-character relationships, and main arcs in this round.
Do not output fragmented products like roster/profile/matrix/arc; do not ask subsequent fragments to complete relationships or arcs for you.
If `character_generation_mode` appears in the context, only treat it as a chain description; do not write it into character fields.

{% if premise %}
## Story Premise (Core Anchor for Character Design)
{{ premise }}
{% endif %}

## Worldbuilding Settings
{{ story_bible | tojson(indent=2) if story_bible is mapping else story_bible }}

(Genre: {{ genre }} | Tone: {{ tone }} | Language: {{ describe_language(language) }})

{% if title %}- Working Title: {{ title }}{% endif %}
{% if expected_total_words %}- Expected Total Words: {{ expected_total_words }}{% endif %}
{% if characters_hint %}- Character Hints: {{ characters_hint }}{% endif %}
{% if conflict_hint %}- Core Conflict: {{ conflict_hint }}{% endif %}
{% if extra_instructions %}- Extra Constraints: {{ extra_instructions }}{% endif %}

{#- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Scale Recommendations and Character Requirements
    --------------------------------------------------------------------------- -#}

{% if expected_total_words %}
Based on this work's scale (approximately {{ expected_total_words }} words):
{% if expected_total_words < 100000 %}
  Recommended 5-7 core characters (core action axis + main pressure source + key relationship/side plot axis + necessary functional roles)
{% elif expected_total_words < 300000 %}
  Recommended 6-10 core characters (core action axis + main pressure source + multiple relationship/side plot axes + necessary functional roles)
{% elif expected_total_words < 800000 %}
  Recommended 8-15 core characters (core action axis + multi-layer pressure sources + multiple relationship/side plot axes + faction/field representatives)
{% else %}
  Recommended 12-20 core characters (core action axis + multi-layer pressure sources + multiple relationship/side plot axes + faction/field representatives)
{% endif %}
{% else %}
Core character count should match the length: short story (<100k words) 5-7 / medium-length (100k-300k) 6-10 / long (300k-800k) 8-15 / epic (>800k) 12-20
{% endif %}

Character Classification: `protagonist` (core main perspective/main action axis) / `antagonist` (main pressure source or opposition axis) / `deuteragonist` (second action axis, relationship axis, or strong side plot axis) / `supporting` (important supporting character, collaboration/obstruction/faction representative) / `minor` (secondary character, no need to set up at this stage)

Core Principles:
- Characters must be consistent with the worldbuilding (era, cultural context, rule constraints)
- `protagonist` represents the most core main perspective/main action axis in the entire book; other equally important characters who carry the second action axis, relationship axis, or strong side plot axis should use `deuteragonist` — do not mark all important characters as protagonist.
- If a dual-core or multi-core structure exists, determine `protagonist` by "who carries the main perspective/main action decisions/chapter advancement responsibility"; the other core typically uses `deuteragonist`. Only output multiple protagonists when the user explicitly requests ensemble multiple protagonists, or when multiple characters truly share the main action axis equally.
- Character hints are not a closed whitelist: retain existing characters and supplement necessary antagonist assistants, faction representatives, and functional roles
- Quality over quantity — each core character must have a clear arc and function; supporting characters should have their own goals and stances independent from the protagonist
- **Avoid protagonist-centrism**: supporting characters should not all revolve around the protagonist; they should have their own goals, stances, and interest conflicts
- **Create faction stratification**: visible forces vs. hidden forces, idealists vs. realists, adding story dimension
- Reserve character "plasticity": some supporting characters should be able to shift stances in subsequent development
- Ending convergence consideration: each core character should receive a reasonable conclusion at the story's end
- Special abilities/backgrounds must comply with the magic_or_tech rules in the worldbuilding

